  "note": "Generated by scripts/contracts/gen-ask-markup-vectors.ts from lib/ask-markup.ts. Do not edit by hand. Prices are decimal strings; pip = 10^-(digits-1) (digits 0/1: 1). WHOLE-POINT SPLIT (owner decision 2026-11-06, replaces rounding each half outward): the markup in points of the last digit, rounded up only if not whole, is split with the ask taking the larger share: askPart = ceil(points/2), bidPart = the rest. accountAsk = raw_ask + askPart, accountBid = raw_bid - bidPart, so the total spread is exactly raw + markup; never tighter than raw and never at or below zero. A BUY opens at accountAsk and CLOSES AT accountBid; a SELL opens at accountBid and closes at accountAsk. The wire carries askMarkup (add to the raw ask) and bidMarkup (subtract from the raw bid). NEGATIVE MARKUP (2026-11-09, raw / zero-spread groups; markup >= 0 is unchanged): the same split with a negative total (askPart = ceil(points/2), bidPart = the rest, both <= 0), so the spread narrows by exactly the markup: candidate ask = raw_ask + askPart rounded up, candidate bid = raw_bid - bidPart rounded down. Client spread = max(0, raw + markup): when candidate bid >= candidate ask, accountBid = accountAsk = (raw_bid + raw_ask) / 2 at the symbol's precision, ROUND HALF TO EVEN. The wire carries the negative askMarkup / bidMarkup; a client applies the same floor.",
